.TH CVEC_APPEND_CVEC 3 "2026-09-20" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cvec_append_cvec \- append one vector onto another (type-inferred, fatal on failure)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cvector.h>

cvec_append_cvec(v_to, v_from);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This macro is a wrapper for cvector_append_cvector(). It calls
ccol_fatal_err() when the append fails. A caller with no useful recovery
for an allocation failure therefore does not need to test a return value.

The macro copies every element of v_from onto the end of v_to, in one bulk
copy. It leaves v_from unchanged. The two vectors then hold independent
copies of the appended elements. The append is all or nothing. Either every
element lands in v_to, or v_to stays exactly as it was.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
v_to    Destination vector. The macro appends to it.
v_from  Source vector. The macro reads it and leaves it unchanged.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The macro stops the program with ccol_fatal_err() when the append fails.
The append fails when the allocation fails. It also fails when the new
element count is more than ccol_max_elem_count.
Both vectors must have the same element size. Two different sizes make
the macro assert. The macro does not report a failure for them.
The macro asserts when one of the vectors is NULL.
An empty v_from succeeds and leaves v_to unchanged.
The macro supports an append of a vector to itself. The content of that
vector then doubles.
The macro copies the elements. It does not move them. A later destruction
of v_from therefore does not disturb v_to. For a vector of pointers, both
vectors then hold the same pointer values, and only one of them can own
the buffers behind those pointers.
Use cvector_append_cvector(3) directly to handle a failed append
yourself. That function does not stop the program.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cvec_construct(a, int);
cvec_construct(b, int);
cvec_push(a, 1);
cvec_push(b, 2);
cvec_push(b, 3);

cvec_append_cvec(a, b);
// cvec_size(a) == 3, cvec_size(b) == 2
cvec_destroy(a);
cvec_destroy(b);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cvector_append_cvector (3),
.BR cvec_append_array (3),
.BR cvec_reserve (3)
